 :activity/id #uuid "53b5db0f-521e-5c61-9c0c-fdff9e2691c7" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049462 :topic/id #uuid "f7488799-2322-5ff9-8065-6852954f5eb5" :topic/math-academy-id 3819} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415579 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415575 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03cdbbac-81f1-5a5a-8c0b-cc9eada2874c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$8$ and $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415544} {:answer/id #uuid "62cb00c2-7471-5b2f-86f0-ee1821df8b74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{3}$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415553} {:answer/id #uuid "903124f2-18ad-506a-90f1-7a04c1d43894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$2$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415559} {:answer/id #uuid "a9a954e9-faca-5755-872b-2adf607495f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415561} {:answer/id #uuid "e9b697fb-7c5f-5191-9456-d6dcf71e2749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{8}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415567}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415567} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ee60de8-7912-55ad-80bc-fd51fae2e264" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415570}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "35756e17-7ddb-5db3-9246-f082e3b776e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-95362" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (8-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =8,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{8} \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "12c4c78d-1201-5f3b-8360-4897312bf437" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415582}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415580 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415578 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a190c4a-9cc2-50ab-a107-16fc3f92fc4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3},\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415545} {:answer/id #uuid "1e594ce1-22ea-5fd6-afb9-6b06b4b9255c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2,\\,1,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415546} {:answer/id #uuid "70323d57-c32e-523a-902e-eb0de24ca0c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3,\\,\\sqrt{3},\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415554} {:answer/id #uuid "83f12e6b-62c0-5595-a194-e0065cfb501d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4,\\,\\sqrt{3},\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415557} {:answer/id #uuid "c6eb0c7d-ecb7-57ee-81fb-a558588e214e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2},\\,1,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415564}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415564} :answer-field/id #uuid "646b1b63-2cd4-5c4d-b0e4-160d844e1954" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415571}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9d417d43-c45e-500b-a5bf-a441848f66ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-95378" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$  \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )((1-\\lambda )^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(1-2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -2) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =2,\\,1,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{1}=1 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "5d5c433e-0023-555a-a2d0-920150952da3"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415581 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415577 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f16480c-d86a-5db9-b802-4ced71c8377c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5},\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415549} {:answer/id #uuid "5febb191-7c5d-5f4e-82d6-efc23b4d4485" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "16,\\,9,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415551} {:answer/id #uuid "73c9cf54-1f9b-52f1-b8ed-dd9e193c12b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9,\\,4,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415555} {:answer/id #uuid "9d3fcfba-14a5-5b55-ba3e-4a632953d6dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3,\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415560} {:answer/id #uuid "be6dbb3a-d9f4-5182-87d2-f89ac41af4ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5,\\,3,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415562}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415560} :answer-field/id #uuid "b838eb18-ab2d-5fe6-b6c3-92ea8e153a8c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9ba2e577-1f2d-586f-a5db-7d03c7c71c22" :question/math-academy-id "q-95375" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-4|\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )[(5-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-4)]-16(4-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda +16)-16(4-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (4-\\lambda )(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,4,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "70681b4b-0f8d-5f23-9042-59cb06bbe55f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415580}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415582 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415574 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22fab31e-219e-5d18-813a-a8d06acc3248" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4,\\,1,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415548} {:answer/id #uuid "7f5778c2-893f-5035-ae58-7208c5dc0a69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4,\\,1,\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415556} {:answer/id #uuid "8e8616be-5d4c-5647-8715-109f64e7adf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2,\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415558} {:answer/id #uuid "c1276a11-417f-5453-89d9-104681d36b19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8,\\,4,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415563} {:answer/id #uuid "cf324114-3726-57f4-b073-13b1533f0488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2,\\,1,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415565}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415565} :answer-field/id #uuid "2503f0e3-6a58-532b-b8da-6c772b852974" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2512d16d-c375-5bf3-9c3b-0ab4d79702bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-95374" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )((2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-4) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -4) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =4,\\,1,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{4}=2 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{1}=1 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "944a1de7-f0ef-562b-9fc3-c518a5f0b063" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415581}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415583 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415576 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "226f1dbb-e586-5c42-93b7-43b8c5544971" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4,\\,3,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415547} {:answer/id #uuid "4f6c601f-dc07-56ea-bef7-25b4a444358f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15,\\,9,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415550} {:answer/id #uuid "6266bf60-cbee-534e-aaad-f1b70c7c6e56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5,\\,4,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415552} {:answer/id #uuid "e2b2ea65-38c0-59e1-8092-216f0cd8d2d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9,\\,4,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415566} {:answer/id #uuid "f993a82a-65cc-57a6-9da0-7876fb553640" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3,\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415568}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415568} :answer-field/id #uuid "9da244a1-6637-5db7-b8ef-33283dce2b41" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415572}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "42bc3fa3-d1ed-5eee-8e63-dbe17bc3a3c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-95349" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )((8-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )-4) & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +36) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,4,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "bd730162-8216-5edd-a4e4-aa3f9eb30275" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415579}}] :activity/title "Computing the Singular Values of a Matrix" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415543}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434793} :activity/id #uuid "f7bf5624-eb3d-524c-adc4-5621731bf40f" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049462 :topic/id #uuid "f7488799-2322-5ff9-8065-6852954f5eb5" :topic/math-academy-id 3819} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434791 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368920 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17453e7d-2501-500c-988d-632cc6dfbc65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$4$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368922} {:answer/id #uuid "3e7fa423-ce11-5e4b-941d-b20daa102519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$8$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368923} {:answer/id #uuid "7cf839ad-4dca-5536-a5e6-2102abbf3175" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$8$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368924} {:answer/id #uuid "d0871187-035d-52b5-b781-f70eaa3bf24c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$4$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368925} {:answer/id #uuid "0183a8ef-a247-5fec-a72f-23430bb57861" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$2$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368926}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368925} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbd50738-594a-50f0-9455-2e79aec8430d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368921}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "80bd1a5b-eef3-57d3-b7a8-ea1d67708737" :question/math-academy-id "q-95364" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}10-\\lambda  & -6 \\\\ -6 & 10-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (10-\\lambda )(10-\\lambda )-36 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-20\\lambda +100-36 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-20\\lambda +64 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -16) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =16,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{16}=4 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0b89f8b4-c620-53dc-98a8-673f79519cb0" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434794}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434792 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368906 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5aacda77-04a2-5890-a544-02a590c4abbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{10}$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368908} {:answer/id #uuid "d7d351a9-304d-59f9-bb2a-64ac42ed426b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$5$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368909} {:answer/id #uuid "37198688-7720-5bf5-9d97-18a4fc4f1eae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$25$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368910} {:answer/id #uuid "11993b50-f9b2-5859-af25-cf8175b4ff5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{5}$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368911} {:answer/id #uuid "4633659c-497d-54ae-9280-c13bf99f6b0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$25$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368912}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368909} :answer-field/id #uuid "08930f82-1a1a-57e2-874c-8663b93ed935" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368907}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "bc0c7469-fdf7-5096-ab3b-9c5617b672e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-95316" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 12 \\\\ 12 & 16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}9-\\lambda  & 12 \\\\ 12 & 16-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (9-\\lambda )(16-\\lambda )-144 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda -16\\lambda +144-144 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-25\\lambda  & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -25) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =25,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{25}=5 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "579fd70b-a4f5-506a-a516-6e2012961957" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434791}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434793 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184878 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea50afa6-cf48-5a28-88f9-d3e965d42d17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$9$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404740} {:answer/id #uuid "58501d70-837f-5aaa-b030-23424dea0d8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{10}$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404741} {:answer/id #uuid "5b30f13e-19e7-5a1b-8f5a-9d9ae0821275" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$3$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404742} {:answer/id #uuid "09c94f4b-6a80-5db2-b8a4-38435a2f0752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$3$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404743} {:answer/id #uuid "185ef847-122c-55fe-afa8-642c48c26e9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$10$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404744}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404743} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1608723-f0ef-5251-b5a7-f10ee403c96e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404739}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1a7c1d3e-ea07-5462-b92b-00ccbee66e53" :question/math-academy-id "q-94982" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )-16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda +25-16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda +9 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{1}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "7fbe2269-e57f-5576-bab4-acdbbf9470a5" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434792}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434794 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385852 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57ba2282-d4ab-5fbf-9130-d06a2eed65a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3,\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385854} {:answer/id #uuid "b45ecc1a-07a7-50a1-a446-cf4a96064ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2,\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385855} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a83de7-3a30-52e2-a29e-09bdd3418bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5,\\,2,\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385856} {:answer/id #uuid "01e6f9da-3643-528a-9879-9df01fb0203d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9,\\,4,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385857} {:answer/id #uuid "d58280f6-ca95-52bf-80d9-6a8986b3c8b